[h1]Languages[/h1][url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/better-elytra-takeoff/README/README.html]EN/English[/url] | [url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/better-elytra-takeoff/README/README_ZH-CN.html]ZH-CN/简体中文[/url]
[h1]Better Elytra Takeoff[/h1]A Fabric server-side and single-player mod that lets players start elytra gliding from the ground with a firework rocket.
[h2]Features[/h2][list]
[*]Use a firework rocket to start gliding from the ground[/*]
[*]Applies the firework boost immediately after takeoff[/*]
[*]Works on dedicated servers and in single-player worlds[/*]
[*]No commands or configuration required[/*]
[/list][h2]Behavior[/h2]When a player uses a firework rocket, the mod cancels the normal use action if the takeoff conditions are met, starts elytra gliding, and spawns the boost rocket.
Takeoff requires:
[list]
[*]Holding a firework rocket[/*]
[*]Wearing a glider item, such as an elytra[/*]
[*]Not sneaking[/*]
[*]Not already gliding[/*]
[*]Not spectating, riding, or creative-flying[/*]
[/list]Aim rule:
[list]
[*]If targeting a block, the player must look horizontally or upward[/*]
[*]If no block is targeted, any look direction can trigger takeoff[/*]
[/list][h2]Supported Versions[/h2][list]
[*]Minecraft 26.1.2[/*]
[*]Fabric Loader 0.19.2+[/*]
[*]Fabric API 0.150.0+[/*]
[*]Java 25[/*]
[/list][h2]License[/h2]MIT
